# Add language-specific patterns when an implementation language is formally approved.
# Python is kept below because Python 3.12 is the current architectural direction
# (see docs/DECISIONS.md). No other language's patterns are assumed yet.

# Python (for a future Python 3.12 component)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# The Window — runtime SQLite database (regenerated automatically on startup)
workspace/events.db

# Builder Agent — runtime status file (regenerated automatically)
workspace/builder_state.yaml

# COO Agent — runtime status file (regenerated automatically)
workspace/coo_state.yaml

# Execution Pipeline — runtime status file (regenerated automatically)
workspace/execution_state.yaml

# Command Bridge — Mission Framework's own live operational data (mission.yaml, messages.yaml, events.yaml, the shared queue file).
# This is ORION's runtime database, not source content: a mission's
# own git commit (see orion/execution/git_manager.py commit()) only
# ever adds the specific deliverable files a handler produced, never
# this directory. Ignored here too as a safety net against `git add -A`
# sweeping test or in-flight mission data into an unrelated commit.
workspace/missions/

# Experience Engine — Knowledge Store's own runtime data (regenerated per mission)
workspace/knowledge/

# Runtime — the resident Runtime's own queue ledger and process state (regenerated on start)
workspace/runtime/

# Intelligence — the project index, graphs, and reports (regenerated by analysis)
workspace/intelligence/
